00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
when i was considering going to college  my 18 year old self was quite  overwhelmed i wasn't sure what exactly i  wanted in a college and i remember  having a lot of conversations with my  dad because he was the one that first  introduced me to hillsdale my mom went  to hillsdale i heard about hillsdale my  junior year my sister went to hillsdale  really saying to him like no dad i don't  want to college i want a university my  cousins went to hillsdale so i was  absolutely opposed to applying here i  heard the spiel it's a christian college  it's hard it takes no government money  that's what my aunt told me well i  visited and i fell in love pretty fast i  really was drawn by the challenge it  presented i need a different sort of  education different sort of training a  different view on what college should be  i wanted to learn how to be a great  leader to be a great person and  hillsdale through their education  definitely teaches you how to do that  and gives you the tools to make you the  best person that you can be  so i get to interview hillsdale  college's president whom i have not yet  met so  i'm nervous to say the least  [Music]  nice to meet you welcome my senior year  i was faced with a lot of options for  college and to be honest i was very  overwhelmed dr arne very overwhelmed it  was one of the most stressful times of  my life how would you describe  hillsdale's approach to education to a  student considering where they should go  hillsdale college was born in 1844  and it is stuck by what it was founded  to do since the beginning we're  interested in  god and we're interested in character  and  freedom and we're interested in learning  and learning of a very high kind the  classic approach is to  begin by defining things you should get  an idea of what college is regardless  what you want from it  it is something it's overwhelmingly  thought of today as preparation for a  job  and that's a very expensive way to go  about it if it however is thought of as  preparation for a good life  then of course it's worth an infinite  price  and so the arts where we approach that  most directly  are the liberal arts  the core curriculum hillsdale college is  the profound thing  that means it's at the foundation down  at the bottom everything built on that  if you get started in the right way  you'll get farther  and so the liberal arts in the core is  the foundation of everything we do here  good job hi dr calvert  oh so good to see you everybody majors  in something right which is important  but hillsdale is also about making sure  that everybody  understands the place of every  department every area of study that  mathematics and philosophy have a lot to  say to one another  history and the sciences have a lot to  say to one another within the minds and  hearts of our students we want them to  understand that this is a unity this is  a whole  yeah you got to have like a foundation  of multiple things to really appreciate  the specific things that you then study  in earnest  built into the college mission is a  specific focus on the western  intellectual and cultural heritage  truth is the object of that heritage  it's about  realizing our full intellectual moral  spiritual and social political humanity  in the end all those things are going to  be crystallized by being here in a  community  that's that's why this is a partnership  that's why this is a college  we wanted that baby  and isabelle and i we're on our way back  from an utter side run utter side is our  favorite ice cream place in all of  hillsdale we made new friends this is  the most midwest thing  i know it's a small school but you still  meet people really cool people all the  time i think the honor code is the  coolest thing ever everyone is going to  be respectful of each other the  friendships that i've made here at  hillsdale are something that has  changed and transformed my life entirely  but i've gotten some teary looks from my  mom  when i say uh yeah i gotta head back  home but i don't really talk about you  know my home in detroit in dearborn i  talk about my home in hillsdale i never  have felt alone at hillsdale there's  definitely a really strong tight-knit  community that you find here that i  haven't found anywhere else the students  here  all come with the same purpose of being  stretched and challenged in new ways  intellectually emotionally  mentally morally spiritually it makes it  easier to go through it when you have  people walking the same path  [Music]  having and expressing faith in god is  becoming increasingly difficult on  college campuses  and so how does faith fit into the mix  at hillsdale college  this was founded as a christian  institution  the reason god has fallen out of favor  it's because we commit a logical  contradiction commonly and that is that  god is bad  or belief in god is bad whereas  there's no definition in any faith or in  philosophy  in which god is not the perfect being  and since we all seek to make ourselves  better  an idea of a perfect being grows  naturally from that activity  and so to exclude god from a college  campus is to exclude its central purpose  there is nothing serious  nothing consequential nothing certainly  noble  about human beings that isn't infused  with its divine origins if you're going  to be serious about being learned  and about being noble  you're going to be serious about god too  i'm going to be completely honest with  you hillsdale can be really challenging  one of the quotes here the only motto is  strength rejoices in the challenge doing  hard things understanding that's a  chance to become a better person and  better yourself through that work i've  grown so much because of your classes i  definitely  would not be as passionate about econ i  think i connect with people who have  gotten better i have a perspective from  that because i was not a good student  but then i fell in love with economics  and i became a good student and so as a  professor i can see students and see the  potential because i know i lived it  strength really does rejoice it doesn't  put up with the challenge it doesn't  resign itself to a challenge it rejoices  in a challenge  it's a curious thing that the serious  study of the liberal arts is an  excellent training for a job because you  learn things that are fundamental to any  job  when i leave hillsdale my career  ambition is to serve in the united  states army as a translator i would like  to go back home to colombia which is  where i'm originally from and to apply  all these things that i've learned here  at hill so back home i am considering  going on to study bioethics practically  i want to illustrate book illustrations  but then also medical illustration i  want to be able to take the lessons that  i've learned here and to apply them to  the world being humble being kind being  patient listening being all the things  that hills are really nurtures and  develops especially in a world that  really gives that a run for its money  first step is cultivate all the virtues  and they are for courage  moderation justice  and wisdom  work on those every day  in the end  you have to get your soul in order both  the moral and intellectual virtues  and that's ultimately the purpose of  education

